      appinfo for a game. (this is useful for games that have asymmetric multiplayer gameplay). }
    procedure SetVRHeadsetStreamingEnabled(bEnabled: Boolean);
    { Returns whether this steam client is a Steam China specific client, vs the global client. }
    function IsSteamChinaLauncher: Boolean;
    { Initializes text filtering, loading dictionaries for the language the game is running in.
      unFilterOptions are reserved for future use and should be set to 0 Returns false if
      filtering is unavailable for the game's language, in which case FilterText() will act as a
      passthrough. Users can customize the text filter behavior in their Steam Account
      preferences: https://store.steampowered.com/account/preferences#CommunityContentPreferences. }
    function InitFilterText(unFilterOptions: UInt32): Boolean;
    { Filters the provided input message and places the filtered result into pchOutFilteredText,
      using legally required filtering and additional filtering based on the context and user
      settings eContext is the type of content in the input string sourceSteamID is the Steam ID
      that is the source of the input string (e.g. the player with the name, or who said the chat
      text) pchInputText is the input string that should be filtered, which can be ASCII or UTF-8
      pchOutFilteredText is where the output will be placed, even if no filtering is performed
      nByteSizeOutFilteredText is the size (in bytes) of pchOutFilteredText, should be at least
      strlen(pchInputText)+1 Returns the number of characters (not bytes) filtered. }
    function FilterText(eContext: ETextFilteringContext; const sourceSteamID: TSteamID; const pchInputMessage: string; pchOutFilteredText: PAnsiChar; nByteSizeOutFilteredText: UInt32): Integer;
